extensions/third-party/pi-codex-conversion/UPSTREAM.md:20:  - **Native deferred-tool serialization (Phase 0, 2026-06-25).** `convertResponsesTools` gained an `emitDeferLoading` option (`providers/openai-responses/shared.ts`) that reads the live fork-core `deferLoading`/`alwaysLoad` flags (cast — absent from the vendored `@earendil-works/pi-ai@0.79.x` `Tool` type) and emits native `defer_loading: true`, mirroring fork core `packages/ai/src/api/openai-codex-responses.ts`. `serializeCodexTools` (`providers/openai-codex/request-body.ts`) enforces the wire invariants fail-closed: any `defer_loading` tool gets a sibling `{type:"tool_search"}` prepended; the colliding FUNCTION `tool_search` (pi-tool-search's discovery tool) is dropped when native search is present (avoids OpenAI 500); kill-switch `PI_CODEX_NATIVE_DEFER=0` reverts to legacy eager serialization (independent of any namespacing flag). Pinned by `tests/codex-deferral.test.mjs`. Without this the fork core's correct emission is dead code for the custom provider and ~27 deferred Codex tools serialize eager (~11k wasted prompt tokens).
